  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis afternoon/evening an upper-level ridge will flatten. This will \nkeep warm temperatures and dry weather across North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana this afternoon. Associated with\nthe upper-level ridge flattening there is modestly strong low- \nlevel and upper-level winds. This will bring breezy conditions to \nthe area this afternoon and evening. On Saturday there will be \nupper-level zonal flow over North-central Montana. This will \nallow the warm and dry conditions to persist. Due to modestly \nstrong low-level and mid-level winds it will also be breezy \nacross North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. On \nSunday upper-level zonal flow persists over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana until Sunday afternoon/evening \nwhen an upper-level ridge builds back in over the area. This will \nbring slightly cooler temperatures to the area with dry weather. \nSmoke from regional wildfires will be around throughout the next \nfew days.\n\nOn Monday and Tuesday the upper-level ridge remains over North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Monday. This will keep warm \nand dry weather for the area on Monday and Tuesday. Wednesday \nthrough next Friday the upper-level ridge remains over North- \ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. Wednesday through \nFriday monsoonal moisture gradually makes it up to Montana. This \nwill bring precipitation chances and cooler temperatures to the \narea Wednesday through next Friday. Wednesday through Friday the \ngreatest forcing is along the Hi-Line and so that is where the \ngreatest chances for precipitation are. See the Forecast \nConfidence & Scenarios section for details. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Saturday there is greater than a 70% chance for wind gusts of\n25 mph or greater across most of North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. On Saturday the HREF (Hi-resolution Ensemble\nForecast) has a 50 - 70% chance for wind speeds of 15 mph or \ngreater and relative humidity less than 20% across much of Fergus \nCounty and portions of Choteau County. Since the majority of the \nzone will not have 15 mph wind speeds and/or consistent wind \ngusts in excess of 25 mph combined with relative humidity less \nthan 20% for three hours and since this is a marginal event at \nthis time a Red Flag Warning was not issued for the Fire Weather \nZone containing most of Fergus and Choteau Counties.\n\nOn Wednesday there is a 30% chance for thunderstorms across the Hi-\nLine and a 15% chance for thunderstorms across the rest of North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. On Thursday and Friday \nthere is a 15 - 30% chance for thunderstorms across most of \nNorth-central Montana. Wednesday through Thursday there is a 60% \nchance for a quarter inch of rain or greater along the Hi-Line. \nAcross the rest of North-central Montana there is a 20 - 40% \nchance for a quarter inch of rain or greater Wednesday through \nThursday. -IG",
